<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Lon Nol</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1913">1913</a>–<a href="/years/1985">1985</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Lon Nol was a Cambodian general and politician who served as defence minister and prime minister under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/norodom-sihanouk">Norodom Sihanouk</a>. On 18 March 1970, while Sihanouk was abroad, he and the national assembly deposed him, and Lon Nol proclaimed the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/khmer-empire">Khmer</a> Republic, becoming its president in 1972. Backed by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a>, his government fought the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/khmer-rouge">Khmer Rouge</a> and North Vietnamese until he fled in April 1975. He died in the United States.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/lon-nol.jpg" alt="Lon Nol" width="320" height="503" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:LonNol.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
